From 4ffa527ecb055bfcf38e4cf3205a0e656513b3d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moojing-jianchuan <jianchuan.lu@moojing.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:42:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(instrumentation): add tap_stage_calls for flattened-VMP
 dispatcher taps

Control-flow-flattened JSVMP bundles funnel every state through one call shape:

    return l.apply(this, [9425].concat(Array.prototype.slice.call(arguments)))

Member/call taps cannot see this boundary: the dispatcher body is opaque, so
when a locally emulated environment diverges from a real browser there is no
per-state evidence to compare. Only the final token differs, and the failure
gives no hint which stage drifted.

This adds `tap_stage_calls` to `instrumentation(action="install")`. It rewrites
that exact shape into `__mcp_tap_stage(<p>, fn, this, arguments, tag, site)`,
which calls the original dispatcher unchanged and records one `tap_stage`
event with the state id (`p`), `argc`, previews of the first arguments, and the
return preview. `action="log"` now aggregates these into `summary.hot_stages`,
and `type_filter="tap_stage"` / `key_filter=<p>` select them.

Design notes:

* Literal match, not AST: it is independent of `mode` and of the
  `filter_property_names` / `filter_object_names` filters, and it still applies
  when the file cannot be parsed. In that case `stats.stage_only` is set and the
  runtime is still injected, so the taps keep working.
* Off by default; existing rewrites, offsets, and behaviour are unchanged.
* Arguments are copied with a captured `Array.prototype.slice` before the call,
  so the tap never mutates the argument list and logging failures cannot replace
  the dispatcher's return value.
* `include_source_site=True` attaches the usual site id for stage taps too.

Verified on a real 315 KB security SDK: 169 dispatcher sites rewritten, 754
`tap_stage` events produced for one `ABC().z(seed, ts)` call (51 distinct
states), and the generated token length is unchanged.
